<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sam Nujoma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1929–2025</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sam Nujoma (1929–2025) was a Namibian nationalist leader and the first president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a>, from independence in 1990 to 2005. He co-founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swapo">SWAPO</a> in 1960 and led its long struggle against South African rule from exile, including the armed struggle that began in 1966. As president he followed a policy of national reconciliation and kept a mixed economy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sam-nujoma.jpg" alt="Sam Nujoma" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ana Nascimento/ABr · CC BY 3.0 br · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sam_Nujoma_(2004)_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
